{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_znhkh73opl6j2odrspl26npnckgr6g3hwjwglpmfgou5yr4s6ajq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **One real translation bug found and fixed.**\n\n## The bug\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `-DNDEBUG`, so the C `.so` imports `__assert_fail` — every `STBDS_ASSERT` is **live**. The Rust made `stbds_assert!` a no-op, documented as \"every assertion holds for all well-formed uses.\"\n\nThat is false. `stbds_hmdel_key` tests `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` *exactly* at lib.c:836/842, but `hm_find_slot` tests `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING`. So with `mode >= 2` and `old_index != final_index`, the post-`memmove` re-lookup passes the element address as the key while still hashing it *as a string* — it hashes the key's pointer bytes, misses, returns `-1`, and trips `assert(slot >= 0)` (lib.c:846).\n\n- **C:** stderr message + `SIGABRT`\n- **Rust (before):** silently indexed `storage[-1]` and wrote through it\n\nFound by the randomized string fuzz row. Fixed by wiring `stbds_assert!` to the same `__assert_fail` with identical assertion text/line/function at all 10 sites; both now die by `SIGABRT` with `lib.c:846: stbds_hmdel_key: Assertion 'slot >= 0' failed.` (only the `__FILE__` directory prefix differs — a build-path artifact).\n\n## Results\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `nm -D` symbol diff | **empty**, 16/16, all 4 configurations |\n| Unresolved non-libc symbols in Rust `.so` | 0 |\n| `CONFIGS.md` — 60 rows | all pass, randomized (fixed seeds) |\n| `ERRORS.md` — 56 rows (E/M/G/A/U) | all pass |\n| Binary driver stdout | no driver exists (library-only `CMakeLists.txt`); `sh_puts` stdout compared byte-for-byte via fd-1 capture |\n| Feature combos × profiles | 4/4 pass — 100 tests each |\n\n`translation/src/lib.rs` is otherwise a faithful translation: the SipHash signed-`int` sign-extensions, the `load_32_or_64` seed recurrence, `arrgrowf`'s growth policy, the arena block-size state machine, and the `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], ...)` struct-in-varargs quirk all match exactly.\n\nArtifacts: `translation/{SYMBOLS,ERRORS,CONFIGS}.md`, tests in `translation/tests/`, and `run_all.sh` (rebuilds both libraries, diffs symbols, runs every feature combo × dev/release). Nothing in `c_src/` was modified.\n\nThree C-side latent bugs are documented as unrunnable (`ERRORS.md` rows U1–U8) rather than tested, since the C itself aborts or corrupts memory on them — notably `shputs` on an existing key, which aliases one `strdup` pointer across two elements and makes the C double-free."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":262,"cache_read_input_tokens":303272,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":262,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61429b9a-98bc-4cd1-a4df-564ad02270a3","uuid":"6078067b-75f3-43df-acd3-d408abcc88b9","timestamp":"2026-09-05T12:16:55.898Z"}
